      "type": "Archive Essay",
      "title": "Long Remote-Sensing Records and the Problem of Temporal Consistency",
      "tags": [
        "Remote Sensing",
        "Time Series",
        "Consistency"
      ],
      "read": "10 min",
      "excerpt": "A decades-long satellite series is rarely one instrument watching continuously. Sensor changes, orbit drift, calibration, fusion, and processing can create trends that look environmental.",
